@model Student

@* LAB 18 — Lab ID: 7 | CHIP_YEAR = 4 | CHIP_LABEL = Final

Model means one Student here because this partial receives one Student,
while Index.cshtml passes a List<Student>.

*@

<tr>
    <td>@Model.Id</td>

    <td>
        <a asp-controller="Students"
           asp-action="Details"
           asp-route-id="@Model.Id">
            @Model.FullName
        </a>

        @if (Model.YearOfStudy == 4)
        {
            <span class="badge bg-success ms-2">Final</span>
        }
    </td>

    <td>
        <year-chip for="@Model.YearOfStudy" />
    </td>

    <td>
        <gpa-badge for="@Model.Gpa" />
    </td>
</tr>


@*

WHAT THE BROWSER RECEIVED:

        <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark" title="rendered by ahmed">Final</span>
(a)
After removing @addTagHelper, the year-chip element appeared in the HTML and the Tag Helper did not execute.

(b)
After removing TagMode, the span was not rendered correctly because no end tag was generated.

(c)
After renaming the element to yearchip, Razor no longer recognized it as a Tag Helper, so it was rendered as a normal HTML element.

All three failures prevented the Tag Helper from producing the expected HTML output.

*@